Method: A block of code that performs an operation.

Constructor: A special class member used to initialize objects.

Instance variable: A non-static variable associated with an object.

Static variable: A class-level variable shared by instances of that class.

Access modifier: Controls access to classes and members.

this: Refers to the current object.

super: Refers to the superclass context.

new: Creates objects or arrays in Java.

Method overloading: Same method name with different parameter lists.

Method overriding: A subclass provides its implementation of an inherited instance method.
